>  <SELECTION_REASON>
Manually reviewed Lewis representation. The crystal contains an N-methyl diphosphine and two ethylene ligands. In the optimized input XYZ, H71 is 2.370 Å from C68, and 1.736 Å from Mo72, C68 to Mo measures 2.164 Å. Each ethylene still has H4. The input geometry supports a methylene/metal hydride limiting form after C–H activation; The crystal record identifies only the parent complex. Localized 24 aromatic-ring bonds using WBOs and original bond lengths. The original paper or deposition identifies the ligands, Checked against the supplied coordinates site by site. The atom order and coordinates of all 76 atoms agree between XYZ and SDF. Lengths of 75 nonmetal covalent bonds: 75 within range, 0 outside range and 0 with sparse controls. Use the supplied Lewis representation for scoring; Independent evidence for the complete graph is limited.

