>  <SELECTION_REASON>
Interactively reviewed graph. Fe–N–O 179.99°, N–O 1.18760 Å, g-xTB N–O WBO 1.6518. The closed-shell assignment for this near-linear terminal ligand is N≡[O+], with metal formal charge +0 and total charge +1. The present +1 species corresponds to {FeNO}⁸ compound 2 in COD 4130130. The authors discuss nitroxyl and predominantly metal-centred reduction using crystallography, isotopic IR, XES and calculations; The +2 crystal with the same skeleton represents another state. Localized 20 aromatic-ring bonds using WBOs and original bond lengths. The atom order and coordinates of all 49 atoms agree between XYZ and SDF. Lengths of 51 nonmetal covalent bonds: 46 within range, 4 outside range and 1 with sparse controls. Examples outside range: 40–42 C-C 1.3633 Å, 21–23 C-C 1.3633 Å, 32–34 C-C 1.3696 Å.

